// TEST: an integer literal beside a float is refused (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3020
// ============================================================================
// The mixing rule (formalism 2.4): nothing converts implicitly. `2` is an
// Int64 and `2.0` a Float64 -- the decimal point is the type -- so `x * 2`
// over a Float64 `x` is refused at the integer literal. Write `x * 2.0`.
// ============================================================================
let x = 2.5
let y = x * 2
